{"id": "live-093", "title": "Solera Multifamily, LLC v. Tegethoff (Old Hickory Village Investor Fraud Suit)", "category": "reit-securities", "status": "pending", "date": "2026-07-13", "jurisdiction": "U.S. District Court, Eastern District of Missouri", "state": "MO", "amount": "~$3M direct investment claim; $540M in Ch. 11 liabilities", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://molawyersmedia.com/2026/07/13/missouri-fraud-complaint-amended-real-estate-case/", "summary": "Magistrate Judge John M. Bodenhausen allowed investors Solera Multifamily, LLC and Hickory Investors, LLC to file an amended fraud complaint against developer Jeffrey J. Tegethoff over the stalled Old Hickory Village apartment project in St. Peters, Missouri, while staying claims against Tegethoff Development, LLC, which sought Chapter 11 protection on June 1, 2026 listing roughly $540 million in liabilities. Creditors in the bankruptcy case have separately moved to install an independent trustee, alleging insider transactions and commingled assets.", "significance": "Shows that a sponsor's bankruptcy filing stays civil fraud claims only against the debtor entities themselves, not against the individual principal or non-debtor affiliates, letting defrauded investors keep pursuing a controlling developer personally while his company's estate is administered separately. Investors and creditors in closely held real estate syndications should watch how the parallel civil and bankruptcy tracks in this case resolve.", "judge": "John M. Bodenhausen", "tags": ["securities fraud", "investor fraud", "missouri", "multifamily", "bankruptcy"]}
